The checker cannot see that a condition this line relies on holds. xs[i] needs i < len(xs), d[k] needs k in d, // and % need a divisor that is not 0, a - b on Nats needs b <= a, and an assert inside a function needs its condition. known(c) gives the proof inside 'if c:' or 'while c:', with c written the same way. Put the code under an 'if' that tests it.
